# {{.Name}} — web app package

Astro (Svelte + Tailwind) frontend embedded in a Go module. The Go app struct
(`{{.Name}}` struct) registers a router over `packages/astro` resolvers and
serves the built frontend from the embedded `dist/`.

## Ports

- App (Go HTTP server): **{{.AppPort}}** — baked in `apps/{{.Name}}/cmd/{{.Name}}`
  and `apps/{{.Name}}/cmd/{{.Name}}-dev`
- Astro dev server: **{{.AstroPort}}** — baked in `astro.config.mjs`

## Development

Recommended: run through the app runner in `apps/{{.Name}}`:

```sh
cd apps/{{.Name}}
make dev    # astro (background) + air hot reload → http://localhost:{{.AppPort}}
make web    # astro dev server only → http://localhost:{{.AstroPort}}
make stop   # stop the background astro server
```

Or run the astro dev server directly from this directory:

```
astro dev --background
```

Manage the background server with `astro dev stop`, `astro dev status`, and
`astro dev logs`. Astro page edits are hot-reloaded; the Go router fetches
the rendered page fresh on every request in dev mode.

## Production build

1. `pnpm build` — renders `dist/`
2. From the repository root:
   `go build -o apps/{{.Name}}/tmp/{{.Name}} ./apps/{{.Name}}/cmd/{{.Name}} && ./apps/{{.Name}}/tmp/{{.Name}}`

The placeholder in `dist/index.html` exists so the package compiles before the
first `pnpm build`.

